  "notes": "The 2017-onward alt-soul template. The tempo mode sits at 116 rather than in the middle of the 61–124 range because the entry says outright that \"the catalogue clusters tightly on **116 and 124**\", and the keys are the named sharp-and-flat church set — B major, F♯ major, A♭ minor and E♭ major. Drums encode a withholding: \"minimal and dry — kick on 1 and 3, a soft rim or clap on 2&4 mixed well down, almost no hat carpet, and long drumless or brush-only passages. When a full kit enters it is on the final chorus.\" So the kick anchors are literally 1 and 3, the snare carries both a clap layer and the cross-stick option, the hat fill density is 0.07 and the velocity tiers are soft. Harmony is \"gospel-jazz: maj7/maj9 tonics, `IMaj7–iii7–vi7–IVMaj7` cycles, secondary dominants, and plagal `IV–I` cadences; 8-bar phrases with real motion, not vamps\" — both families are the entry's own, reduced to degrees, and the harmonic rhythm keeps moving rather than vamping. The load-bearing melodic claim is unusual and is what `motifPitchCount` and the counter encode: the melody is \"habitually sung in **block harmony rather than as a single line** — model 3-to-6 stacked parts moving in parallel as the melody itself\", so the counter is an octave stack at −12 with a high density ratio rather than an answering lick. Bass is \"warm and simple, root motion in 8ths with wide rests; light sub-doubling. No 808 slides\" — a kick mirror at a very high root probability, and no `bass808` block, because the entry rules the slides out and a sub that doubles a played bass is not an 808 part. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum number and all melody figures; the research marks the drum detail as inference.",
